WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Applause]  two a.m. on November 9th 2016 I was  alone in the middle of the street  shouting at the top of my lungs Donald  Trump had just been announced as the  next president of United States I was  overcome by emotion and the shouting was  helping it was helping release some of  that emotional pressure I had been  feeling you know what people a lot of  people felt a lot of things that day  some people were ecstatic  finally a president had been elected  that really understood their needs and  others were really sad how could someone  who had been so divisive once for me  those feelings that night those shouts  were all about anger I was angry because  of the uncertainty I knew a trump  presidency would bring from my own  country Mexico I've thought a lot about  that night what I did but I could have  done and you know what I would have done  if I could go back I would have gone  into a library and I would have brought  some regressions today I'd like to tell  you why with the hope that maybe by  telling you the way I dealt with those  emotions it can help you figure out how  to deal with the emotions you might be  saying I was born and raised in Mexico I  grew up in a family that has always  believed that the Mexico the Mexican the  US should be closer together my dad was  the chief architect and negotiator for  Mexico the North American Free Trade  Agreement I came to study college in the  u.s. I worked here after that I am about  to graduate from two masters degrees  here in the US I came to study and work  in the United States because I hope to  live a life that allows me to bring the  two countries closer together  I love Mexico and I have a profound  admiration for the United States for me  it's always been obvious that bringing  our two countries closer together it's a  good thing and yet Donald Trump seems to  stand for completely the opposite of  that I was so angry that night because I  couldn't help but feel that he had won  precisely because he had promised to  divide our two countries  he's literally promised to build a wall  between our two countries and that made  me angry I was desperate to take action  to do something but I didn't know what  to do so instead I started expressing my  emotions in all kinds of platforms  whatsapp Facebook emails in front of  people anything that I could do to share  how I was feeling I shared how I was  angry how I hated that the US was doing  this to us I even said I hated the US  and to be honest all of Mexico started  doing the same and suddenly the  discourse in Mexico towards the United  States changed in a way that it hadn't  changed in over three decades anti-us  feelings became the norm an extreme  left-wing presidential candidate who is  incredibly anti us is now the  frontrunner for the presidential  elections in our country people started  calling for US companies to be kicked  out of Mexico for tariffs to be imposed  on us imports people started calling for  mexico to push the u.s. out  when I saw that all that anger I had  been feeling became work suddenly  despite everything I had been feeling  and saying I realized that pushing the  u.s. out was not the right course of  action no what we needed was finding  ways to keep letting the u.s. in and so  I set out to prove that with data I  suddenly had something to do wasn't the  most exciting action but it was some  action it consisted in locking myself up  in a library looking at data sets and  running regressions you know we can  think of what NAFTA did and two big  things one was that it lowered US  tariffs  for Mexican products those are the  tariffs that Donald Trump has threatened  to raise the second thing it did is that  it lowered Mexican tariffs for u.s.  products now Donald Trump gets to decide  what he wants to do with his tariffs but  we as Mexico we get to decide what we  want to do with ours and so the question  for me was what should we do with our  tax should we raise them and push the  u.s. out or should we keep them at zero  and keep letting the US come in the  answer wasn't obvious spent a lot of  days in the library but suddenly I  figured out I was able to show that  Mexico has grown much more because  Mexico lowered its tires from the US  products then because the u.s. lowered  its hours on us that means that free  trade has been good for Mexico that  means that businesses in our country  have grown because we opened up to the  u.s. that means that we shouldn't push  the u.s. out but rather keep finding  ways to let them in  running those regressions gave me  clarity I suddenly knew what I had to do  I had to find ways for Mexico in the  u.s. to keep even close to one another  even if my feelings were telling me not  to do that we are all feeling a lot of  things these days these are emotional  times some of us are facing the most  challenging issues many of us have ever  seen and it's hard to overcome the  emotions we're feelings sometimes they  can paralyze us and other times they can  jump it into action that we maybe  haven't fully thought out so today I  want to ask you to compliment those  emotions and those feelings with data  and analysis if you're feeling paralyzed  jump into the data of whatever it is you  care about I may be that analysis will  give you clarity on how to move forward  and if you're already jumping into  action then maybe pause for a moment and  make sure by looking at the data that  what you're doing is going to help if  you're marching and protesting keep  marching and protesting but make sure  you have the data to back that up when I  start preparing to give this talk a  couple months ago my intent was to argue  that the way we can counter the  inflammatory and outrageous statements  made by someone like Donald Trump by  being equally outrageous and  inflammatory ourselves and while that  might feel good for an instant it's not  going to do anything No  today more than ever we need to focus on  facts on data on analysis so the next  time that you're feeling like you want  to go run some regressions thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

